Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:23:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] fix(auth): require providerId claim in verified
 Supabase token
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to the signature-verification fix: after verifySupabaseJwt, the
providerId (sub) claim must be present before it is used as a unique key for
account lookups. Missing sub now yields a validation error instead of an
undefined-key Prisma query.

Validation: cd server && npx tsc --noEmit; npx jest.

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
---
 server/src/services/auth.service.ts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/src/services/auth.service.ts b/server/src/services/auth.service.ts
index e6986ff..7fa8b0b 100644
--- a/server/src/services/auth.service.ts
+++ b/server/src/services/auth.service.ts
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ export class AuthService {
 
     const { email, sub: providerId, user_metadata } = decoded;
 
-    if (!email) {
+    if (!email || !providerId) {
       throw new ValidationError({ email: ['Supabase token payload does not contain an email'] });
     }
 
